    "q-37356": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37356",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $B$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =-5$ is an eigenvalue of $B$\n\nII. $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $B$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )((3-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )+10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda +3)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7$, we have that the only real eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-3$ (both with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
